  "name": "Example: Integrating an Exponential Function With a General Base",
  "problem": "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int -6(7^x) \\, \\textrm d x.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we factor out the constant $-6.$ Then, we integrate the exponential function, and get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\int (-6)7^x  \\, \\textrm d x   \n&= -6\\int 7^x\\,\\textrm{d}x\\\n&=-6 \\cdot \\dfrac{7^x}{\\ln 7} + C.\n}\n$$",
